\title{AKCatchments: Delineate and Characterize Alaska Stream Catchments with Documented Uncertainty}
\description{
Delineates the catchment draining to a stream point anywhere in Alaska from the best available elevation data (by default the statewide 5 m IfSAR bare-earth terrain model), checks each delineation for the failure modes that automated D8 routing is prone to, compares it with reference flowlines, hand-drawn catchments and USGS StreamStats, and always draws it on satellite imagery so it can be checked by eye. Summarises topography, climate, snow, land cover, permafrost, geology, soils, fire history and alder cover for each catchment, carrying the uncertainty of every value in companion columns, and links daily stream temperature records compiled by AKTEMP.
